---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms">
  <div class="screen">
    <div class="page-head reveal">
      <div>
        <h1>Terms and conditions</h1>
        <p>Last updated 5 November 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="legal grow scroll">
      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        Iris lets developers define plugins and lets users turn them on to have questions answered about their
        new emails. By using Iris you agree to these terms and to our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your account</h2>
      <p>
        You sign in with Google and are responsible for activity on your account. You can delete it at any time
        from <a href="/subscriptions">your subscriptions page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Developers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep your API keys secret. We show each key once and cannot recover it.</li>
        <li>Use answers only for the purpose your plugin describes, and do not try to rebuild users' emails from them.</li>
        <li>Do not build plugins that deceive users or collect passwords, payment details or other secrets.</li>
        <li>Follow the law, including privacy law, for any data you receive.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not abuse the API, get around rate limits, probe for vulnerabilities without permission, or use Iris
        to harm others. We may suspend accounts or plugins that do.
      </p>

      <h2>Answers are automated</h2>
      <p>Answers come from a model and can be wrong. Do not rely on them for legal, medical or financial decisions.</p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        Iris is provided as is, without warranties of any kind. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable
        for indirect or consequential losses, or for lost data, profits or revenue.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and ending</h2>
      <p>
        We may change or stop the service and these terms. We will update this page and its date; using Iris
        after a change means you accept it.
      </p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Iris is created and run by Sreyash Satpathy. Email
        <a href="mailto:f20250721@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in">f20250721@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
